  "id": "COMPOUND:17121 - PROTEIN:5848",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a relationship between the compound [(3R,4R,5R,8S,9S,10R,13S,14S,17S)-17-[(1S)-1-(dimethylamino)ethyl]-10,13-dimethyl-3-[methyl(3-methylbut-2-enoyl)amino]-2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-tetradecahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-4-yl] acetate and the Raji cell line. This compound is identified as a target for multiple pathways, including microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is a well-characterized target of several compounds, including 5,7-Dihydroxy-8-(3-Methylbutanoyl)-6-(3-Methylbut-2-Enyl)-4-Propylchromen-2-One, CID 11603911, and Petroraspailyne B1. These compounds are known to interact with microtubules, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving microtubule inhibition. The presence of multiple targets for the same compound, all leading to Raji, indicates a possible role in modulating microtubule dynamics in these cells. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism of action involving microtubule-associated proteins, and the compound appears to be a potential candidate for targeting Raji cells through this pathway.",
